RandomEffectsController
=======================

MIXED lib. Runs random span events (script commands 6 and 7,
.docs/protocol.md § C) on random_effects_task. The dispatch loop hands
each span over with Submit(); the task keeps the span table and posts each
due change to servoQueue / gpioQueue as an ordinary type-1 / type-5
command; panic and config reload call StopAll(). The decisions themselves
(span building, the move rule, the table) are PURE and native-tested in
lib_native/AstrOsRandomEffects; this lib adds the queue, the lock and the
logging around them.

It is the pilot for extracting a domain from src/main.cpp (CLAUDE.md,
"Extracting a domain from main.cpp"): main.cpp keeps only the Init call,
the task-create line and one-line calls where the domain is triggered.

Classification
--------------

MIXED: includes <freertos/...>, <esp_log.h>, <esp_timer.h>, <esp_random.h>.
Does NOT compile under [env:test].

Threading
---------

- The span table and the clear fence are touched only under the
  controller's table mutex: by random_effects_task, and by StopAll (panic
  on interfaceResponseQueueTask, reload on serviceQueueTask).
- The task never holds the table mutex while waiting on another lock: the
  Maestro channel read (main.cpp's readMaestroChannel, which takes
  maestroModulesMutex and the module's stateMutex) happens before the take.
- Changes are posted while the table mutex is held, so a StopAll that has
  taken it sees no post after its Clear().

Queue ownership
---------------

The controller owns its queue at both ends. Submit mallocs the command
copy and frees it if the send fails; the task frees it after processing;
StopAll's drain frees what it removes. Change strings posted to
servoQueue / gpioQueue follow the CLAUDE.md convention: the controller
mallocs and frees on a failed send, and the queue consumer frees after
processing.
